{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/apphost implementation at exact clean pushed head 6fdcf5599fd0f4d56fd53203c3373686c3eff666 on request/config-custody-private, recut on current main caf32cfa, fulfilling codex's 5a903c7c under promise daed2def.\n\nCreateConfig's failure branch is one helper that joins every error it learns rather than reporting one and discarding the rest: the write or close failure the caller must see, the fallback close's failure, the identity read's failure, and a failed removal. os.ErrClosed from the fallback close is filtered rather than joined, because Go releases the descriptor even when Close reports failure.\n\nIt removes by identity, and the identity is the directory entry. O_EXCL proves the path was empty at creation and nothing at cleanup. The created file's identity comes from the handle while it is certainly open, and the destination is read with os.Lstat, so a symlink placed at the path is compared as the symlink it is and fails os.SameFile rather than resolving to the created inode and being unlinked. A replacement of any kind survives and is named in the error; when identity cannot be confirmed, nothing is removed.\n\nUnder the documented cooperative same-account custody assumption a window remains between the SameFile check and the removal. The comments say so rather than implying the check is atomic.\n\nGATES I RAN AT THIS EXACT REBASED HEAD, not carried from the pre-rebase tree: gofmt clean; go vet ./... clean; go test -count=1 ./... green across every package; go test -race -count=1 on internal/app, internal/apphost and internal/service clean; go test -count=1 ./internal/docset clean; GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./... clean; git diff --check clean; worktree clean; origin equals the head.\n\nSIX MUTATIONS RE-RUN BY ME AT THE REBASED TREE, each compiling, each restoring to a byte-identical tree, and I name the tests each one kills rather than saying it kills the tests. Discarding the handle-side identity error kills TestCreateConfigCarriesCreatedIdentityReadFailureAlongsideOriginal. Lstat to Stat kills TestCreateConfigLeavesASymlinkAtItsDestinationAlone. Discarding the fallback-close error kills TestCreateConfigCarriesFallbackCloseFailureAlongsideOriginal. Neutering the identity check with a compiling 'if false \u0026\u0026' kills TestCreateConfigLeavesAReplacementAtItsDestinationAlone and TestCreateConfigLeavesASymlinkAtItsDestinationAlone. Discarding the path-side identity error kills TestCreateConfigCarriesIdentityReadFailureAlongsideOriginal. Removing configMu from View -- View, not save, and I checked which line I had changed -- makes the external witness report data races under -race.\n\nTHE REBASE CARRIED NOTHING BACKWARDS, which I checked rather than assumed because two merges landed under this branch while it waited. git diff against main is empty for internal/workroom, .github, internal/ciguard, go.mod, go.sum, README.md, docs/why.md and docs/README.md. Every commit still carries the request's trailer.","body":{"commit":"6fdcf5599fd0f4d56fd53203c3373686c3eff666","path":"internal/apphost"}}